{% set local_problem %}
<p>Owens Cross Roads has significant terrain variation — from relatively flat areas to properties on hillsides. That terrain affects how water behaves after it leaves your downspouts. Dump water uphill from your foundation and it runs right back toward your house. Dump it on a slope and it can cause erosion.</p>

<p>Many homes have downspouts placed wherever was convenient during construction, not wherever was best for drainage. The result is water pooling near foundations, eroding landscaping, and seeping into basements and crawlspaces.</p>

<p>Proper downspout design considers your specific terrain and uses it to advantage — directing water downhill, away from your home, to safe discharge points.</p>
{% endset %}

{% set service_explanation %}
<p>Downspout services include: proper sizing for your roof area; strategic placement considering terrain; extensions to move water away; secure mounting; and underground connections for invisible drainage.</p>

<p>We assess your property's specific situation and design a system that works with your terrain.</p>
{% endset %}

